    <headline>Heavy Rain Risk Area</headline>
    <description>The high-pressure system covers the upper North and the upper Northeast while the easterly wind and the southeasterly wind bring the moisture from the South China Sea to the eastern part of the Northeast and the East. Meanwhile, the monsoon trough lies across the Gulf and the South. 

Less rains is likely in the upper country while isolated heavy rains are forecast in the eastern part of the Northeast and the East the South while and isolated heavy rain are forecast in. 

For the Andaman Sea and the Gulf, waves will be higher than 2 meters high in thundershower areas. 

</description>
    <instruction> People in these area should beware of heavy rains and accumulations that may cause flash flood and overflows, especially along the waterways near foothills and lowlands.  All ships should keep off thundershowers. </instruction>
    <web>https://www.tmd.go.th/en/forecast/daily</web>
